    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my bosch dishwasher is showing an E15 error code. i looked at the manual but i'm not really sure what i'm doing. how do i check the leak sensor and get the bottom of it dry?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "An E15 error on a Bosch dishwasher indicates a detected water leak in the sump, so inspecting and drying the leak sensor is the correct first step to try. Look under your dishwasher's front panel in a well-lit area to locate the small, spring-loaded metal lever or cup that houses the sensor at the bottom of the tub. You can safely attempt to manually compress the spring lever or rotate the sensor cup to tilt and drain any accumulated moisture out onto a towel, as long as the unit is unplugged. If the sensor remains stuck or you cannot drain the water effectively, your dishwasher may need professional service to replace the faulty component.",
