      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You might not need to fully disassemble the unit; try using a long flexible funnel and a small electric hand blower or air duster to quickly blow any standing water out of the sensor cup and filter area through the filter gap. If you can't reach it visually, manually rotate the bottom-actuated lever inside the sump using a long screwdriver while pushing through the small service window to tilt the sensor naturally. Should the water pool behind a filter or gasket is easily accessible through the filter, remove the bottom filter and lightly clean debris from around the sump area. This usually clears the sensor enough to reset the E15 code without major part replacement.",
