    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, water can appear out of nowhere in small, confined spaces like the filter area or drain pump hole if there is a clog preventing water from escaping, causing pressure that forces it out later. It is very likely the issue isn't just a dry sensor but a blockage in the drain path or the pump itself that traps water, which eventually causes the leak sensor to activate again once the system attempts to pump. Before risking further internal work, check the main filter and spray arms for obstructions, and verify that the drain hose isn't kinked or inserted too deeply into the drain溝. Please consider calling a professional technician if you cannot find the blockage, as forcing tools into a blocked drain could damage seals or create water damage.",
